  "summary": "Talk about breakfast: say what you eat and drink, and give the food the object ending -an.",
  "intro": "Week 3 is all about food and drink, and today starts with breakfast. To say what you eat or drink, put the food after the verb: آكُلُ خُبْزًا (I eat bread), أَشْرَبُ شَايًا (I drink tea). The food is the object of the verb, so in careful Arabic it takes the ending -an, written as two fathas (tanwīn).",
  "objectives": [
    "Name ten breakfast foods and drinks",
    "Say what you eat and drink with آكُلُ and أَشْرَبُ",
    "Put the object ending -an on a noun: خُبْزًا, قَهْوَةً",
    "Ask a man or a woman what they eat in the morning"
